1
00:00:00,589 --> 00:00:04,775
(Q1) Jacinta: Hello, Easy Life Cleaning Services, Jacinta speaking.

2
00:00:04,775 --> 00:00:05,856
Client: Oh hello.

3
00:00:05,856 --> 00:00:10,814
I'm looking for a cleaning service for my apartment - do you do domestic cleaning?

4
00:00:10,814 --> 00:00:11,638
Jacinta: Sure.

5
00:00:11,638 --> 00:00:14,549
Client: Well, it's just a one-bedroom flat.

6
00:00:14,549 --> 00:00:17,013
Do you have a basic cleaning package?

7
00:00:17,013 --> 00:00:17,945
Jacinta: Yes.

8
00:00:17,945 --> 00:00:23,306
For a one-bedroom flat we're probably looking at about two hours for a clean.

9
00:00:23,306 --> 00:00:28,906
So we'd do a thorough clean of all surfaces in each room, and polish them where necessary.

10
00:00:28,906 --> 00:00:37,741
[Q1答案句] ：Does your apartment have carpets?Client: No, I don't have any, but the floor would need cleaning.Jacinta: Of course - we'd do that in every room.

11
00:00:37,741 --> 00:00:41,182
And we'd do a thorough clean of the kitchen and bathroom.

12
00:00:41,182 --> 00:00:41,695
Client: OK.

13
00:00:41,695 --> 00:00:55,686
(Q2) [Q2答案句] Jacinta: Then we have some additional services which you can request if you want - so for example, we can clean your oven for you every week.Client: Actually, I hardly ever use that, but can you do the fridge?Jacinta: Sure.

14
00:00:55,686 --> 00:00:57,604
Would you like that done every week?

15
00:00:57,604 --> 00:00:59,006
Client: Yes, definitely.

16
00:00:59,006 --> 00:01:03,378
(Q3) And would ironing clothes be an additional service you can do?

17
00:01:03,378 --> 00:01:04,656
Jacinta: Yes, of course.

18
00:01:04,656 --> 00:01:08,409
[Q3答案句] Client: It wouldn't be much, just my shirts for work that week.

19
00:01:08,409 --> 00:01:09,234
Jacinta: That's fine.

20
00:01:09,234 --> 00:01:16,843
[Q3干扰项] And we could also clean your microwave if you want.Client: No, I wipe that out pretty regularly so there's no need for that.

21
00:01:16,843 --> 00:01:22,983
(Q4) Jacinta: We also offer additional services that you might want a bit less often, say every month.

22
00:01:22,983 --> 00:01:29,217
[Q4答案句] So for example, if the inside of your windows need cleaning, we could do that.Client: Yes, that'd be good.

23
00:01:29,217 --> 00:01:37,105
[补充说明（～=废话）] I'm on the fifteenth floor, so the outside gets done regularly by specialists, but the inside does get a bit grubby.

24
00:01:37,105 --> 00:01:55,113
(Q5) [Q5答案句：干扰项-否定表达-提出新疑似答案-确认表达] Jacinta: And we could arrange for your curtains to get cleaned if necessary.Client: No, they're OK. But would you be able to do something about the balcony?It's quite small and I don't use it much, but it could do with a wash every month or so.Jacinta: Yes, we can get the pressure washer onto that.

25
00:01:55,113 --> 00:02:01,545
(Q6) Jacinta: Now if you're interested, we do offer some other possibilities to do with general maintenance.

26
00:02:01,545 --> 00:02:13,450
[Q6答案句] For example, if you have a problem with water and you need a plumber in a hurry, we can put you in touch with a reliable one who can come out straightaway.And the same thing if you need an electrician.

27
00:02:13,450 --> 00:02:14,619
Client: Right.

28
00:02:14,619 --> 00:02:15,437
That's good to know.

29
00:02:15,437 --> 00:02:20,771
I've only just moved here so I don't have any of those sorts of contacts.

30
00:02:20,771 --> 00:02:34,465
(Q7) [Q7答案句] Jacinta: And I don't know if this is of interest to you, but we also offer a special vacuum cleaning system which can improve the indoor air quality of your home by capturing up to 99% of all the dust in the air.

31
00:02:34,465 --> 00:02:37,995
[Q7空前定位词] So if you're troubled by allergies, this can make a big difference.

32
00:02:37,995 --> 00:02:38,906
Client: Right.

33
00:02:38,906 --> 00:02:42,774
In fact, I don't have that sort of problem, but I'll bear it in mind.

34
00:02:42,774 --> 00:02:46,104
(Q8) Now can you tell me a bit about your cleaning staff?

35
00:02:46,104 --> 00:02:47,522
Jacinta: Of course.

36
00:02:47,522 --> 00:02:50,946
So all our cleaners are very carefully selected.

37
00:02:50,946 --> 00:03:02,215
[Q8答案句] When they apply to us, they have to undergo a security check with the police to make sure they don't have any sort of criminal background, and, of course, they have to provide references as well.

38
00:03:02,215 --> 00:03:06,898
(Q9) [Q9答案句] Then if we think they might be suitable for the job, we give them training for it.

39
00:03:06,898 --> 00:03:12,092
That lasts for two weeks so it's very thorough, and at the end of it, they have a test.

40
00:03:12,092 --> 00:03:23,810
(Q10) [Q10答案句] If they pass that, we take them on, but we monitor them very carefully - we ask all our clients to complete a review of their performance after every visit and to email it to us.

41
00:03:23,810 --> 00:03:27,434
So we can pick up any problems straightaway and deal with them.

42
00:03:27,434 --> 00:03:30,084
Client: OK, well that all sounds good.

43
00:03:30,084 --> 00:03:33,366
And will I always have the same cleaner?

44
00:03:33,366 --> 00:03:38,089
Jacinta: Yes, we do our best to organise it that way, and we usually manage it.

45
00:03:38,089 --> 00:03:38,889
Client: Good.

46
00:03:38,889 --> 00:03:39,769
That's fine.

47
00:03:39,769 --> 00:03:42,269
Right, so I'd like to go ahead and …

